Only the both-nexioms-needed rule is left, because all three one-nexiom pairs contained ruseso or kutupok. The 4 remaining pairs are:
- {ruguni, vutorel}
- {sifulal, ruseso}
- {sifulal, vutorel}
- {ruseso, vutorel}

One test can only give two outcomes, so the best I can do is split these 2/2 and then guess between two. Testing ruguni, sifulal and vutorel does this:
- **Lit:** the pair is {ruguni, vutorel} or {sifulal, vutorel}.
- **Dark:** the pair is {sifulal, ruseso} or {ruseso, vutorel}.

TEST: ruguni, sifulal, vutorel
